  "title": "Verbs and Making Sentences",
  "description": "The verb \"to be\", the eight verbs you need most, and the pattern that turns them into sentences.",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "u9l1",
      "title": "To be",
      "goal": "Say what something is — and what it is not.",
      "notes": [
        "The verb changes with the subject: main ... han, tu ... hain, uh ... hai, asin/tusin ... han/ho.",
        "To negate, put nahin directly before the verb: uh vadda nahin hai."
      ],
      "items": [
        {"id": "u9l1-01", "pa": "ਹਾਂ", "roman": "han", "en": "am / are (with main, asin)", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l1-02", "pa": "ਹੈ", "roman": "hai", "en": "is", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l1-03", "pa": "ਹਨ", "roman": "han", "en": "are (plural)", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l1-04", "pa": "ਹੋ", "roman": "ho", "en": "are (with tusin)", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l1-05", "pa": "ਸੀ", "roman": "si", "en": "was / were", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l1-06", "pa": "ਨਹੀਂ ਹੈ", "roman": "nahin hai", "en": "is not", "kind": "phrase"},
        {"id": "u9l1-07", "pa": "ਮੈਂ ਖੁਸ਼ ਹਾਂ", "roman": "main khush han", "en": "I am happy", "kind": "phrase"},
        {"id": "u9l1-08", "pa": "ਉਹ ਵੱਡਾ ਹੈ", "roman": "uh vadda hai", "en": "He / it is big", "kind": "phrase"},
        {"id": "u9l1-09", "pa": "ਇਹ ਛੋਟਾ ਹੈ", "roman": "ih chhota hai", "en": "This is small", "kind": "phrase"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u9l2",
      "title": "Eight useful verbs",
      "goal": "Learn the dictionary form of the verbs you will use most.",
      "notes": [
        "The dictionary form always ends in -na: jana, aauna, karna. That is the \"to ...\" form.",
        "Drop the -na and add -da/-di + han to make \"I do X\": bolna becomes main bolda han."
      ],
      "items": [
        {"id": "u9l2-01", "pa": "ਜਾਣਾ", "roman": "jana", "en": "to go", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l2-02", "pa": "ਆਉਣਾ", "roman": "aauna", "en": "to come", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l2-03", "pa": "ਕਰਨਾ", "roman": "karna", "en": "to do", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l2-04", "pa": "ਬੋਲਣਾ", "roman": "bolna", "en": "to speak", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l2-05", "pa": "ਸਮਝਣਾ", "roman": "samajhna", "en": "to understand", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l2-06", "pa": "ਦੇਖਣਾ", "roman": "dekhna", "en": "to see / to look", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l2-07", "pa": "ਸੁਣਨਾ", "roman": "sunna", "en": "to listen / to hear", "kind": "word"},
        {"id": "u9l2-08", "pa": "ਸਿੱਖਣਾ", "roman": "sikhna", "en": "to learn", "kind": "word"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u9l3",
      "title": "Building your own sentences",
      "goal": "Put subject, object and verb together — and negate them.",
      "notes": [
        "Word order: who - what - verb. main panjabi bolda han = I / Punjabi / speak.",
        "Once you can swap the middle word, you can say hundreds of things with the verbs from the last lesson."
